.TH XYMONAPI-CONNECT 1 "November 2, 2026" "xymon-plugins"
.SH NAME
xymonapi-connect \- connect this machine to the Xymon API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymonapi-connect URL [NAME]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
xymonapi-connect gets this machine a token of its own for the
.I xymonapi(8)
at URL, so that the programs reading the API from here send that token and
no password. It is installed with the API's client, by
\fB./install.sh install xymonapi\fR, and run once per machine and API.

In order, it:
.IP 1. 4
reaches the API and checks its certificate, and stops there, asking
nothing, when this machine does not trust it, saying where to copy the
server's certificate;
.IP 2. 4
keeps a token from an earlier run while it still works;
.IP 3. 4
otherwise, when the API asks for a password, asks for a user of the API
(XYMONAPI_USER when set) and the password once, on the terminal, or as two
lines on stdin when stdin is not one; gets with them a token for this
machine, named by its short hostname; and writes it to
~/.config/xymon-api/NAME.token, mode 600. The password is not kept;
.IP 4. 4
says when the API and this client run different versions of xymonapi, and
who can act on it: the server's admin when the API is the older, this
machine when the client is;
.IP 5. 4
prints on stdout what a client needs, as shell settings: XYMONAPI_URL,
XYMONAPI_TOKEN_FILE when there is a token, and XYMONAPI_CA when a
certificate is used.
.PP
Given the API's own socket, unix:PATH, on the server, it asks nothing and
keeps nothing: the socket's permissions decided already who connects, and
the settings printed name the socket alone.
.PP
Running it again changes nothing while the token works, and replaces one
that was revoked. Messages go to stderr. A password file an earlier setup
kept, ~/.config/xymon-api/NAME.password, is removed.

NAME, xymon by default, tells one API from another: each has its own token
file. The API's /tokens lists this user's machines and revokes one.

.SH OPTIONS
.IP URL
The API's address as other machines reach it: http:// or https://, the
host, and the port when it is not the scheme's own -- 1986 for the API's own
HTTPS, the web server's for one in front of it -- without /xymon/api/v1,
which the client adds; or
unix:PATH, the API's own socket on the server, $XYMONVAR/xymonapi/api.sock
unless xymonapi(8) was told otherwise, for a program on that machine.
.IP NAME
Letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-', 64 at most.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_USER\fR"
The user of the API, not asked.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_CA\fR"
The certificate, or the CA, to trust for an https:// URL. The default is
~/.config/xymon-api/NAME-ca.pem when that file exists: copy the server's
certificate there, over a channel already trusted. Verification is never
turned off.
.IP "\fBXYMONAPI_PYTHON\fR"
The Python to run with. Unset, the python3 of the virtualenv beside the
plugins, $PREFIX/libexec/xymon-plugins/venv, which \fB./install.sh venv\fR
makes, when there is one; else the first of python3, python3.14 down to
python3.9, found on PATH. Nothing is
asked: this program needs no module beyond the standard library.
.IP "\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR"
Where xymon-api/ is, ~/.config by default.

.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when this machine is connected; 1 when the API cannot be reached, its
certificate is not trusted, or it refused the password; 2 for a wrong
argument; 130 when interrupted; 77 without Python 3.9, or when the run with
the python3 on PATH is declined.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
xymonapi(8), xymonapi-mcp(1), xymonapi-rag(1)
